                                        "sense_id": "8b8ba4a4-2644-3615-b380-e00902f0b0e7",
                                        "entry_id": "bb2be68b-4799-3aa0-9916-677525732be6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quilted skirt worn by women."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "158ab31b-1318-3d75-907b-faf3d4b87813",
                                        "entry_id": "bb2be68b-4799-3aa0-9916-677525732be6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something composed of a variety of stitched-together parts; a patchwork."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b06d8d7-e0f5-4b0c-8435-92f6a35d0ede",
                                                "sense_id": "158ab31b-1318-3d75-907b-faf3d4b87813",
                                                "text": "Her humor was as bawdy as ever, and evenly placed throughout. Early on […] she alternated alternated jokes and stanzas, providing a wonderful quilt of her musical and story-telling talents."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "quilt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "281bbf5a-39ec-3a36-86ba-eb27c284063b",
                                        "entry_id": "3891231e-7325-3956-8fee-bb4c83854408",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To construct a quilt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "986de458-22fe-36a5-be08-ba98cb6f5c9c",
                                        "entry_id": "3891231e-7325-3956-8fee-bb4c83854408",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To construct something, such as clothing, using the same technique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e22b7ec-f6e3-46c2-96de-1a7da681e1df",
                                                "sense_id": "986de458-22fe-36a5-be08-ba98cb6f5c9c",
                                                "text": "Get up, get up for shame, the blooming morne / Upon her wings presents the god unshorne. / See how Aurora throwes her faire / Fresh-quilted colours through the aire; / Get up, sweet slug-a-bed, and see / The dew bespangling herbe and tree."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20476f22-4f2c-4d01-98a1-53bfe19c9fd4",
                                                "sense_id": "986de458-22fe-36a5-be08-ba98cb6f5c9c",
                                                "text": "Two hundred Sempſtreſſes were employed to make me Shirts, and Linen for Bed and Table, all of the ſtrongeft and coarſeſt kind they could get; which, however, they were forced to quilt together in ſeveral Folds, for the thickeſt was ſome degrees finer than Lawn."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0d88437-a338-3f68-bf0f-e997515973d2",
                                        "entry_id": "3891231e-7325-3956-8fee-bb4c83854408",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To beat or thrash."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "625647ed-151b-4e05-8a62-e6fff8c322f8",
                                                "sense_id": "a0d88437-a338-3f68-bf0f-e997515973d2",
                                                "text": "I am glad, said Mr. Slick, that cussed critter, that schoolmaster, hasn't yet woke up. I'm most afeerd if he had aturned out afore we started, I should have quilted him, for that talk of his last night sticks in my crop considerable hard."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b1cc1080-1ad5-44ef-bc40-ef5866440665",
                        "source_entry_id": "9db8909c-4a79-3ed0-9f63-fbbb44491e21",
                        "source_sense_id": "fac104c7-516f-39a2-b7a2-0d249aaf3f67",
                        "target_lang_word": "eiderdown",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eiderdown",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7957a243-b552-347b-b2b9-3b8607d422f1",
                                        "entry_id": "0547e62f-f269-38aa-807d-cf10064bc1ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The down of the eider duck, used for stuffing pillows and quilts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "297b2b7c-ec53-4220-b727-7877132d88be",
                                                "sense_id": "7957a243-b552-347b-b2b9-3b8607d422f1",
                                                "text": "A great sea lifted us high and, crashing down with a deafening roar, carried us swiftly along on light foam as soft as eiderdown."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e3422ee5-a3d3-3c97-9e6a-cfc8d36b2f6f",
                                        "entry_id": "0547e62f-f269-38aa-807d-cf10064bc1ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quilt stuffed with this down."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04ad8922-1061-4729-8339-3e06cd707c41",
                                                "sense_id": "e3422ee5-a3d3-3c97-9e6a-cfc8d36b2f6f",
                                                "text": "The landlord was near spraining his wrist, and I told him for heaven’s sake to quit—the bed was soft enough to suit me, and I did not know how all the planing in the world could make eider down of a pine plank."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0182c28-25fa-4865-b09e-d99fa1141777",
                                                "sense_id": "e3422ee5-a3d3-3c97-9e6a-cfc8d36b2f6f",
                                                "text": "I entered. It was a very small room, overcrowded with furniture of the style which the French know as Louis Philippe. There was a large wooden bedstead on which was a billowing red eiderdown, and there was a large wardrobe, a round table, a very small washstand, and two stuffed chairs covered with red rep."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12d74ba4-bb4e-45d3-82b6-8148a51e6713",
                                                "sense_id": "e3422ee5-a3d3-3c97-9e6a-cfc8d36b2f6f",
                                                "text": "She jerked up in bed, clutching the eiderdown; her heart beat. What could it be?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
